{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'first non-\"'`:finally`|first enclosing `:handler`|''^'\"\\\\| \\\\*\\\\*P[023]′' docs/design/yang.preludes.md\"","aggregated_output":"205:- **Unwind traversal semantics (r8):** `raise` delivers to the first non-`:finally` boundary; on the way down every `:finally` frame runs its cleanup closure **exactly once**, and every `:effect` frame is popped with its context restored (an `:effect` frame carries no cleanup closure — a guest throw crossing an unrelated effect handler is a plain unwind past it, never an error). `perform` walks `ctx-cell` to the nearest matching `:effect` frame **without** running `:finally` frames; only when the handler aborts without resuming does the abort path run the traversed `:finally` cleanups during that unwind. In all cases the context is restored to the surviving frame's state and each cleanup runs at most once per activation.\n213:| **Abortive control (exceptions & escapes)** | `raise` | `[ctx-cell e on-empty]` | Unwind `:finally` frames passing `e`; `:effect` frames are popped with context restored (no cleanup closure — a throw crossing an unrelated effect frame is a plain unwind past it); deliver `e` to the first enclosing `:handler` (or non-`:finally` boundary frame); call `(on-empty e)` if empty. **One rule per frame kind (r8):** `:finally` → run cleanup exactly once, continue unwinding; `:effect` → pop, restore, continue unwinding; `:handler`/boundary → deliver and stop. Gate: a throw past an unrelated effect frame with exactly-once cleanup. |\n645:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`/`clj`-family) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\n647:| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Native collection invocation through the new standard library (the locally-bound-map `:k` → 9 fixture) and bundled primitive shadowing of bare `get`/`assoc` (which otherwise resolve through the source store before VM primitives); unified `yang.clojure` suite green. The real `clj → clj.py → clj` cross-syntax unwind (cleanup + context restoration) gates ONLY at P3′, after `clj.py` exists. |\n648:| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legacy `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `runtime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-host `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deterministic `str`/`gensym`); capability refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); default-profile regressions (r8): an unqualified `:k` key admits successfully (the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only); equal exact integers in different host carriers hit the same map entry on insert AND lookup; a local/projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` remains distinguishable from an absent binding; canonical traversal order matches Jing encoded-byte order (`0` before `nil`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
