{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '/\"'^ *[0-9]*[[:space:]]*### 7.5/,/Cell-safe collection predicates/p'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"   568\t### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n   569\t\n   570\tIn Slice P3, the portable Clojure standard library splits into two Layer-2c linker modules — eliminating store-key collisions against VM primitives while publishing cell-free 0-arg export accessors:\n   571\t\n   572\t1. **`clojure.core.impl` (pure, stateless implementation module — banned from `:ambient-projections`):**\n   573\t   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n   574\t   - **Zero bare primitive store collisions:** Every definition is prefixed `impl-*` (`impl-identity`, `impl-get`, `impl-assoc`, `impl-conj`, etc.), so internal calls to `(get m k)`, `(assoc m k v)`, `(conj xs x)`, `(first xs)`, `(rest xs)`, `(vec xs)`, `(nil? x)`, `(empty? xs)`, `(not b)` resolve directly to VM primitives.\n   575\t   - **Cell-safe collection predicates:** `impl-cell-ref?` ensures authenticated callable cells answer **`false`** to all of `coll?`, `map?`, `set?`, `vector?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, and `reduced?`; `impl-fn?` matches `clj/admitted-callable?` 1-to-1.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
